# Pipeline 3 (Production) - Environment Variables
# Every variable below is actually read by pipeline3_production/src code
# (verified by grep for process.env.* — none are aspirational). Copy to
# .env and fill in values only for the features you need; the test suite
# (npm test) requires none of these — it runs entirely on injected fixtures.

# --- P3.08-DIST Distributed Render (Kaggle) — required only if you call
# P309Orchestrator.phase3Execution / orchestrateFullWorkflow without
# passing an explicit `identity` override. Read by src/p309Config.ts.
# No default account/repo is baked into source — omitting these causes
# loadP309Identity() to throw with an explicit error, not a silent
# fallback to someone else's Kaggle account. (NOT related to phase P3.09
# Automated QA — see the naming note in src/orchestration_p309.ts.)
KAGGLE_USERNAME=your_kaggle_username
P309_GITHUB_REPO_URL=https://github.com/your-org/your-fork.git

# Real Kaggle CLI submission/auth itself (kernels push, datasets create) is
# NOT configured here — the `kaggle` CLI binary reads its own credentials
# from ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json (see https://www.kaggle.com/docs/api). This
# applies to both P3.08-DIST distributed render and P3.10 Kaggle delivery
# (src/kaggle.ts) — this codebase only shells out to `kaggle`, it never
# reads a Kaggle API key from process.env.

# --- P3.08-DIST Live Execution Script (src/p309_live_execution.ts) —
# optional. This is a standalone manual verification script, not part of
# the library API or the test suite. Defaults shown match the script's
# original hardcoded paths.
# P309_REAL_VIDEO_PATH=/tmp/pipeline_video_final.mp4
# P309_OUTPUT_DIR=/tmp/p309_live_results
# P309_WORKING_DIR=/tmp/p309_execution

# --- P3.08 Remotion Render — optional. Read by src/render.ts. If unset,
# Remotion falls back to its own managed/downloaded browser.
# REMOTION_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE=/opt/pw-browsers/chromium

# --- P3.05 ElevenLabs Production Voice — this codebase does NOT read an
# API key from process.env itself: generateProductionVoice() (src/elevenlabs.ts)
# takes apiKey as an explicit function parameter, supplied by whoever calls
# runP305ElevenLabsProductionVoice(). If your integration wires that
# parameter from an environment variable, ELEVENLABS_API_KEY is a
# reasonable conventional name, but nothing in src/ reads it directly.
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=your_elevenlabs_api_key_here
